<title>CANADA: Canada May natural gas production rises 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada May natural gas production rises 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Tuesday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    May 1997     May 1996	 pct</p>
<p>   Production   9,155.1	9,625.3	 -4.9</p>
<p>   Exports	5,976.5	5,276.5	+13.3</p>
<p>   Imports	3,462.1	3,211.2	 +7.8</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 7,168.0	7,616.7	 -5.9</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   May 1997     May 1996	  pct</p>
<p>   Production  13,020.6     12,813.1	 +1.6</p>
<p>   Exports	6,663.6	6,727.1	 -0.9</p>
<p>   Canada sales 4,909.7	4,647.1	 +5.7</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL (thousands of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Jan-May 1997  Jan-May 1996   pct</p>
<p>   Production     47,790.6   47,638.4	+0.3</p>
<p>   Exports	  27,575.2   25,985.6	+6.1</p>
<p>   Imports	  17,720.8   16,494.5	+7.4</p>
<p>   Ref receipts   38,378.7   38,181.8	+0.5</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>   Production     66,355.8   64,484.2	+2.9</p>
<p>   Exports	  34,357.7   33,469.7	+2.7</p>
<p>   Canada sales   34,211.5   33,599.3	+1.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Eleonore Harding, Energy Section, (613) 951-5708.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
